Systematic taxonomy of cellular automata (CAs) 
-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
A unified family tree for:

	better cross‑family mapping
	clearer genotype/phenotype tools
	more interdisciplinary coherence

Five major families — asynchronous, stochastic, multi‑state, extended‑neighbourhood, and non‑uniform 
— and analyzing each through definition, variations, genotype, phenotype, and applications. It aims 
to replace the fragmented CA literature.

1. Classical CA Framework (the baseline)
-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
The classical CA as a sextuple  

	𝐶=⟨𝑇, 𝑆, 𝑠, 𝑠_0, 𝑁, 𝜙⟩
  
with:

	𝑇 	— tessellation (grid)
	𝑆 	— finite state set
	𝑠 	— output function giving cell state at time 𝑡
	𝑠_0 	— initial condition
	𝑁 	— neighbourhood
	𝜙 	— local update rule

This induces a global update rule Φ on the configuration space.

